<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35979" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phĕnĕos</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φένεος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Arcadia</i>, <i>with a lake of the same name</i>, <i>the fabled
				Stygian waters</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15, 332</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 28,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8, 165</span></i>.—The city is
			called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phĕnĕum</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 6,
				10, § 20</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phĕnĕātae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φενεάται</span>, <i>the
				inhabitants of Pheneüs</i>, <i>the
				Pheneans</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 3, 22, 56</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 6, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
